My suggestion is to find a StorageWorks BA350 box and a HSD05 or HSD10 
DSSI (to SCSI) controller and some RZ*-VA disks and of course a cable 
from the rear panel to the HSD05/10. That setup would give you the 
possibility to use the most modern disks (up to six disks). You should 
be able to find all those components on Ebay for a small amount of money.
I doubt that the BA23 power supply can provide enough power for directly 
connected disks.

If you decide to go for this solution, I can make a list of the needed 
parts (if you don't want to find out that by yourself).

